title ALES151 — Lotus's stereo_pad_tail: the padded top-and-tail carried into stereo, one margin of joint silence for both channels, bound to ALES150 by the pad-zero law
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Second rung this turn. After landing ALES150 stereo_top_tail and sending it, the ascending Lotus crux is ALES99 (pad_tail — the padded top-and-tail, keep a chosen margin of silence at each end) carried into stereo. Crux-first and Lindy-first agree: pad_tail is the one honest parameter every recorder and DAW adds to its silence trim, and the natural companion to the flush stereo trim just landed.
think The wall is the one ALES148/149/150 all met: padding each channel by its own silence would give the two speakers different margins and lengths and tear the stereo image apart, because ALES147 proved the two channels segment independently. So the rung keeps ONE margin for both — the leading and trailing JOINT silence (a run of frames .silent in both channels), kept up to pad and cut for the excess, identically from both channels. The content bracket is exactly ALES150's (the union of the two speakers' outer content, first-to-last not-jointly-silent frame); the leading joint silence is every frame before it, the trailing every frame after.
think Implementation mirrors mono pad_tail (ALES99) lifted the same way stereo_top_tail lifted ALES98: segment both channels up front through ALES147 (all validation, empty-clip BadFrame → both untouched), forward pass finds first_ns/last_ns, compute lead_silence=content_start and tail_silence=original-content_end, keep min(pad, available) at each end, cut trailing excess first then leading, both channels in lockstep, postcondition asserting both hold content+margins and leave balanced. StereoPadTailError = ALES150's StereoTopTailError reused whole (pad has no illegal value). Pad-zero proven against ALES150's flush trim across eight frame lengths, four floors, three splits; margin law against a second independent by-hand reference across eight pads.
obs No custody gate reached — purely local, two bounded i16 Clips, a self-approved design round. First-try witness GREEN, no red this round. Recorded lesson: a mono parameter that keeps a margin of the SAME kind of silence the trim removes (pad_tail keeps min(pad, silence)) lifts to stereo by keeping the margin of the JOINT silence — the shared run the trim already removes — so the margin is identical on both channels and balance holds for free; the pad-zero law binds it to the flush trim (ALES150) as ALES99 is bound to ALES98. Witness GREEN (pad-zero, margin, known-pad, full-pad-unchanged, monotone, all-joint-empty, no-joint-unchanged, four atomicity refusals), width-check exit 0, dense asserts (not on the zero-assert ratchet). Front door lotus/README.md synced (ALES151 roster entry appended to the Status line).
loom witness=ales_stereo_pad_tail_witness result=GREEN laws=2-crux channels=2 class=stereo-edit read=reads-through-segmenter+edits-in-lockstep form=keep-margin-of-joint-silence decision=silence-intersection-at-ends cases=pad-zero-law(=ALES150-flush,8flen*4floor*3split)+margin-law(=by-hand-padded-span,8pads,min(pad,avail))+known-pad(frame4-floor500-pad2=len20)+full-pad-unchanged+monotone+all-joint-empty+no-joint-unchanged+atomicity(empty,ragged,inverted-band,illegal-floor) reds=0
file lotus/stereo_pad_tail.rye ALES151 — stereo_pad_tail, the padded top-and-tail lifted to stereo: keep min(pad, available) of the leading and trailing JOINT silence, cut only the excess from both channels in lockstep (tail first); stereo_top_and_tail_pad, StereoPadTailError = ALES150's StereoTopTailError reused whole; bound to ALES150 by the pad-zero law.
file tools/ales_stereo_pad_tail_witness.rish the witness — three-say (Language/Style/Lens), builds, runs selftest, asserts the GREEN ales-stereo-pad-tail line.
file active-designing/20260815-054529_fill-ales151-lotus-stereo-pad-tail.md the self-approved design read for this rung — the crux, the wall, the shape, the two laws.
file lotus/README.md front door synced — ALES151 roster entry appended to the Status line.
recommend keep-going the stereo edit corner grows on the silence readers; the next ascending Lotus crux is ALES100 (collapse_silence — shrink every interior silent run to a fixed length) carried into stereo, then ALES101 (smooth_runs) and ALES102 (smooth_trim) — crux-first, agent-doable, no gate reached, witness GREEN, width-check exit 0.
